  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Selgantolimod and Keratin, type I cytoskeletal 9, based on shared targets in a network involving Magnesium levulinate. Selgantolimod is implicated in targeting multiple entities, including Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A and Plasma kallikrein, which in turn are targets of Magnesium levulinate. This pathway leads to the targeting of Keratin, type I cytoskeletal 9, indicating a possible indirect interaction between Selgantolimod and this keratin subtype through the intermediary of Magnesium levulinate. The scores across all three paths are consistent, suggesting a robust association, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a network-level relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Selgantolimod and Keratin, type I cytoskeletal 9.",
